          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            is called a
            %em free field theory
            if it describes standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            of fields without any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+field+theory"} interacting field theory
          %p
            There is some freedom in formalizing precisely what this means. At the very least the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of a free field theory should be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+differential+equations"} linear differential equations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+field+theory"} relativistic field theory
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"} Lorentzian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            one typically requires that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+differential+equation"} linear differential equation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation+of+motion"} of motion
            is, after
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+equation"} wave equation
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_covariant_phase_space_geometrymultisymplectic_geometry In covariant phase space geometry/multisymplectic geometry
          %p
            We describe free field theory in the language of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+spaces"} covariant phase spaces
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lagrangians"} local Lagrangians
            and their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+geometry"} multisymplectic geometry
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ;
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma = (\mathbb{R}^{d-1;1}, \eta)
            be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi σ
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma^i \;\colon\; \Sigma \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
